<b>Fukuo Yui</b>

00:21:48.090 --> 00:21:53.850
<b>Hirose Yuki</b>

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.660
<i>with A-O-P's Hirose Yuki...</i>

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:52.880
<i>And Fukuo Yui.</i>

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:57.680
<i>Even when it comes to comfortable cycling, 
if you ride your bike the wrong way...</i>

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:02.000
<i>"I can't take it anymore! My hips hurt!"</i>

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:06.420
<i>"My shoulders are really stiff."</i>

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:13.430
<b>Riding Comfortably: Proper Riding Posture</b>

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:11.970
<i>This time we'll learn proper 
riding posture for your bike.</i>

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:19.430
Could you teach us how to ride bikes in 
a way that prevents strain on our bodies?

00:22:18.480 --> 00:22:21.940
<b>Y's Road Ochanomizu
Manager Yamada Yunosuke-san</b>

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:24.730
Since I have a bike here, let's see what 
you can do by actually getting on the bike.

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:25.480
Okay.

00:22:25.480 --> 00:22:27.420
I'll ride, then.

00:22:28.080 --> 00:22:30.130
First, take hold of the handles.

00:22:30.130 --> 00:22:30.740
Okay.

00:22:30.740 --> 00:22:33.180
This is a normal riding posture.

00:22:33.180 --> 00:22:35.560
At first, riding with your 
arms fully extended—

00:22:33.180 --> 00:22:39.460
<b>At first, riders tend toward riding with their arms fully extended</b>

00:22:35.560 --> 00:22:36.280
Like this?

00:22:36.280 --> 00:22:41.750
Yes, people tend towards that position.

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:46.290
It's very easy, but because it uses lots 
of small muscles, it can't be sustained.

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:52.390
<b>Elbows Extended
Only allows use of small muscles in the arms and causes fatigue</b>

00:22:46.290 --> 00:22:47.240
Really? It can't be?

00:22:47.240 --> 00:22:52.390
It's a very tiring posture for long rides,

00:22:52.390 --> 00:22:55.700
so if you're prioritizing riding 
comfortably for a long time,

00:22:55.700 --> 00:22:56.970
you should bend your elbows.

00:22:57.350 --> 00:22:58.730
It causes you to lean forward,

00:22:58.730 --> 00:23:01.710
but it allows you to use the 
large muscles in your stomach

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:08.360
<b>Elbows Bent
Allows use of stomach and back muscles and reduces fatigue</b>

00:23:01.710 --> 00:23:03.780
and back which have staying power,

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:07.580
allowing you to ride comfortably 
for long periods of time.

00:23:06.560 --> 00:23:08.360
Really?

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:11.650
Good, good. Yes.

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:11.220
Am I doing it right?

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:14.720
Wow, that looks right.

00:23:14.720 --> 00:23:19.970
In this posture, if you have muscles here,
you could keep pedaling forever.

00:23:19.970 --> 00:23:22.320
My arms are completely relaxed.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:26.090
But in this posture,
they're tensed the whole time.

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:32.660
It does seem like you'd be able to 
ride longer by using these muscles.

